ial_handling\"\n\n    # Long routes keep the previous classification, but add extra context.\n    # This is a simple condition without an else branch.\n    if checkpoints > 3:\n        status = status + \"_long_route\"\n\n    # Return the final classification after all rule checks.\n    return status\n\n```\n\nPrevious proposed answer:\n```python\ndef test_classify_delivery_boundary_behavior():\n    result = classify_delivery(5, 100, False)\n    assert result == \"heavy\"\n```\n\nValidation error:\nAssertionError: assert 'light' == 'heavy'", "response": "```python\ndef test_classify_delivery_boundary_behavior():\n    result = classify_delivery(6, 100, False)\n    assert result == \"heavy\"\n```", "duration_sec": 20.598}
